_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible from Godot 4.5 to Godot 4.6 rc2\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8088) - AMD Ryzen 5 7600 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 31.74 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn Godot 4.5 all Control nodes got a new \"Accessibility\" tab where users can add a \"Name\" and \"Description\" for control nodes so that screen readers can have that information, but when setting up a translation .POT file, these fields are not being pulled into the .POT when they really should be.\n\nWhen I opened a discussion about this one user mentioned that:\n\"the name and description are translated but don't get extracted because the POT generator hasn't been adjusted\"\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a UI button on a brand new Godot project, then give it some text, and in the accessibility tab give it a \"Name\" and a \"Description\". When generating a .POT file you will notice only the text is present for the button, not the Name and Description.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNA","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/org